# Mastra Changelog 2025-06-13 | Mastra Blog

Another busy week at Mastra. The team has been largely heads down, making moves on some big projects (big updates coming very soon 👀.) But that doesn't mean we've slowed down on shipping core platform improvements.

Let's dig in…

## [Cross-Thread Memory Recall![](https://mastra.ai/_next/static/immutable/media/anchor.3595n93ztlxu8.svg)](https://mastra.ai/blog/changelog-2025-06-13#cross-thread-memory-recall)

We added cross-thread semantic recall functionality to Mastra Memory, allowing memory retrieval across different threads belonging to the same resource, via a new `scope` key that can be set to `resource`.

```
const agent = new Agent({
  memory: new Memory({
    options: {
      semanticRecall: {
        topK: 3, // Retrieve 3 most similar messages
        messageRange: 2, // Include 2 messages before and after each match
        scope: 'resource', // Search across all threads for this user
      },
    },
  }),
});
```

Agents can now access memories from previous threads when working with the same user or resource. The 'resource' scope is currently supported by LibSQL, Postgres, and Upstash storage adapters.

## [Output Schema Support for Agents![](https://mastra.ai/_next/static/immutable/media/anchor.3595n93ztlxu8.svg)](https://mastra.ai/blog/changelog-2025-06-13#output-schema-support-for-agents)

We previously sanitized input schemas with the `@mastra/schema-compat` utility. Now, we've extended that to support output schemas as well.

In addition, we've enabled support for any Zod schema (not just Zod objects) when you stream or generate objects. For example, you could generate an array.

## [Other Updates![](https://mastra.ai/_next/static/immutable/media/anchor.3595n93ztlxu8.svg)](https://mastra.ai/blog/changelog-2025-06-13#other-updates)

*   **Enhanced Workflow Observability**: Added log filtering with level-based filtering (debug, info, error) and infinite scrolling for workflow execution logs in the local playground ([#4706](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4706 "Visit https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4706"), [#4768](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4768 "Visit https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4768")).
*   **Unified Developer UI Experience**: We're pulling some of the things we've done in Mastra cloud into the local playground for better consistency between Playground and Cloud UI. This includes simplified navigation structure and enhanced agent page layouts ([#4524](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4524 "Visit https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4524")).
*   **MCP Prompt Support**: Added support for MCP prompts to both `MCPServer` and `MCPClient` ([#4566](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4566 "Visit https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4566")).
*   **Storage API Pagination**: Implemented pagination support across PostgreSQL, MongoDB, and Upstash, with new paginated `getEvals` method ([#4652](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4652 "Visit https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4652"), [#4631](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4631 "Visit https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4631")).
*   **LanceDB Vector Integration**: Added LanceDB as a new vector database provider option with `MastraVector` and `MastraStorage` interfaces ([#3324](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/3324 "Visit https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/3324")).

Find the full release log [here](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/releases/tag/%40mastra%2Fcore%400.10.4 "Visit https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/releases/tag/%40mastra%2Fcore%400.10.4").

# Mastra Changelog 2025-05-29 | Mastra Blog

MCP Server updates, streaming support, and more.

It’s been an eventful past few weeks at Mastra. Last week we shipped [Mastra 0.10](https://mastra.ai/blog/mastra-0.10 "Visit https://mastra.ai/blog/mastra-0.10"). Yesterday we publicly announced the [hackathon winners](https://mastra.ai/blog/mastra-build-recap "Visit https://mastra.ai/blog/mastra-build-recap"). And today we’re back with more updates.

Let’s dig in…

## [Pass agents into MCPServer![](https://mastra.ai/_next/static/immutable/media/anchor.3595n93ztlxu8.svg)](https://mastra.ai/blog/changelog-2025-05-29#pass-agents-into-mcpserver)

Agents can now be directly passed into the MCPServer class, automatically creating tools from them (with the naming convention `ask_<agentId>`.) The agent description is converted into a tool description and the tool will call `agent.generate()`.

## [Pass workflows into MCPServer![](https://mastra.ai/_next/static/immutable/media/anchor.3595n93ztlxu8.svg)](https://mastra.ai/blog/changelog-2025-05-29#pass-workflows-into-mcpserver)

Similarly, you can also pass workflow instances into the MCPServer class. This gives you a tool for each workflow. The workflow `inputSchema` and description are used as the tool `inputSchema` and description. Calling the tool will start the workflow.

## [Stream workflows![](https://mastra.ai/_next/static/immutable/media/anchor.3595n93ztlxu8.svg)](https://mastra.ai/blog/changelog-2025-05-29#stream-workflows)

We added streaming support (`stream`) for workflows so users can see exactly what step an executed workflow is on.

```
const { stream } = run.stream({inputData: {}))
for await (const data of stream) {
  if (data.type === 'step-suspended') {
    // make it async to show that execution is not blocked
    setImmediate(() => {
      const resumeData = { stepId: 'promptAgent', context: { userInput: 'test input for resumption' } };
      run.resume({ resumeData: resumeData as any, step: promptAgent });
    });
  }
}
```

This works similarly to the client-js watch SDK.

## [Other updates![](https://mastra.ai/_next/static/immutable/media/anchor.3595n93ztlxu8.svg)](https://mastra.ai/blog/changelog-2025-05-29#other-updates)

*   [We now support MongoDB as a storage backend](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/3841 "Visit https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/3841"). [You can also pass options to MongoDBStore, similar to how options are passed in the Vector case](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4414 "Visit https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4414").
*   [We added configuration for the `mastra` package in the Verdaccio registry setup for E2E testing environment](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4393 "Visit https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4393").
*   [We added runtimeContext to evals.](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4422 "Visit https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/4422").

That’s all for this week. Happy building 🚀

